The tests above stub the HTTP layer, which leaves out the retry policy, and that
is what decides how long the user waits.
So here we use the real client against a port where nothing listens, recording
the sleeps of the retries instead of sleeping them.
What varies is who needs the request: a precaution gets one try, and a request the
caller depends on still gets all of them.

